["er.request/1",{"definition_version":1,"fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"intent":{"causation":null,"command_id":"cmd-child-045583d86fcfaf245ecf8eac6bad613e2940e5636130146d86cb96fdb647796f","command_type":"aep.entity.create/v1","correlation_id":"protocol-artifact-new","execution_id":null,"expected_revision":null,"payload":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nA publication that fails after staging removes its stage directory, so no\n`.engineering/planning.aep-stage-*` directory is ever left beside the projection by a refused\nrender, write or validate.\n\n## Why\n\n0.59.0's refused `render` left a full stage of the projection (33 to 467 files) in each of the\nsix cut-over repositories; a `git add -A` would have committed it. 0.59.2 removes the stage on\nthe fall-through it added, but the other error returns after `stage()` in `publish_current`\n(`crates/plan/aep-planning-migration/src/projection.rs`) still return without removing it.\n","status":"draft","title":"A failed publication leaves no stage directory beside the projection"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/a-failed-publication-leaves-no-stage-directory"},"target":null,"task":null},"result":{"affected":["ent-e2bda3df1908e7b2d5370fc70f681ac1@1"],"audit":["aud-fb3c80bb3b0ee27fc7d58384eac65df4"],"command_id":"cmd-child-045583d86fcfaf245ecf8eac6bad613e2940e5636130146d86cb96fdb647796f","consistency":"seq-000000000000","events":["evt-fb3c81bb3b0ee432c7d58684eac6630d"],"outcome":"accepted"}},"lifecycle_state":"recorded"}},"kind":"create","recording":{"actor":"human:timo","causation":"cmd-child-045583d86fcfaf245ecf8eac6bad613e2940e5636130146d86cb96fdb647796f","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","record_id":"aep.applied:child-045583d86fcfaf245ecf8eac6bad613e2940e5636130146d86cb96fdb647796f@1~63c8bee0d911e289","recorded_at":"2026-09-24T20:29:59Z"},"subject":["aep.applied","child-045583d86fcfaf245ecf8eac6bad613e2940e5636130146d86cb96fdb647796f"]}]